  message: "DIAGNOSED 2026-09-09, same day as filing. This item's stated first task was\n\"why the fixture said otherwise\". Answered, and the answer makes this cell far\ncheaper than 0-of-40,970 suggests.\n\n**SCALA IS JAVA BEFORE PR #227.** Read in\npackages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/scala.py,\nthe external method-call branch (~line 1083):\n\n    gate_meta: dict = {\"call_construct\": \"method\"}\n    receiver_type = var_types.get(receiver_name) if receiver_name else None\n    if receiver_type:\n        gate_meta[\"receiver_type_hint\"] = receiver_type\n    edges.append(Edge.create(\n        src=current_function.id,\n        dst=f\"scala:external:0-0:{callee_name}:unresolved\",   # <-- HARDCODED\n        ...\n        meta=gate_meta,\n    ))\n\n**The module segment is a hardcoded literal `external`, even on the branch that\nhas just computed the receiver's type.** scala DOES track types -- `var_types`\nis populated from parameter annotations and val/var declarations -- and DOES\nstamp `receiver_type_hint`. The type is routed ONLY to meta, for the Tier-2\n`inherited_calls` linker. It never reaches the module slot, which is what\n`_match_propagation_entry` reads.\n\nSo the fixture was not wrong about EMISSION, and neither was WI-nasuf: scala\nemits, and stamps `call_construct: \"method\"` correctly. What the fixture could\nnot see is that the slot the F3 gate reads is a constant.\n\nTHIS IS VERBATIM THE JAVA DEFECT THIS CLASS ALREADY FIXED. INV-linub's own\n2026-08-06 entry: \"java = emission works but the module segment carries the\nVARIABLE NAME while the receiver TYPE it already computes (var_types) is routed\nonly to meta[receiver_type_hint] for Tier-2 linkers. That last one is the\ncheapest fix available.\" PR #227 routed it into the slot and produced the first\nlegitimate method-kind sink match in the nine-language table. java now measures\n65.0% typed on killbill. scala is the same shape, one language over, unfixed --\nLIVE.md rule 1 (CHECK THE SIBLING LANGUAGE) firing exactly as it did for\nWI-lajus earlier today, where the whole fix was cpp's and already shipped.\n\nTHE SANITIZER GUARD PR #227 NEEDED IS ALREADY PRESENT HERE. That PR had to\nclose a channel it opened: naming the type also SHORTENS the callee, and\n`_register_sanitizer_callers` matches on the short name, so a first-party\n`doFinal` bound the catalogued `javax.crypto.Cipher.doFinal`, and a phantom\nbarrier earns `sanitized` and DROPS the flow (#214). Its guard was\n`call_construct`, and **scala already stamps `call_construct: \"method\"` on this\nexact branch.** Read in taint.py, `_register_sanitizer_callers` honours\n`call_construct == \"method\"` and consults the module slot.\n\nBUT THAT IS ALSO THE HAZARD, AND IT IS THE OPPOSITE OF THE OBVIOUS ONE. That\nfunction's own docstring says the placeholder \"still yields no module, and is\nstill refused\". Filling the slot with a real type is precisely what makes those\nregistrations REACHABLE for scala for the first time. So this fix opens the\nsanitizer channel rather than leaving it closed, and more registered barriers\nmeans more `sanitized`, which DROPS flows. **Measure at L4 on findings, both\nsigns, before and after.** WI-lajus, the same day, is the live cautionary case:\na typed-receiver win that moved 15 of 21 claim verdicts toward withholding.\n\nPRE-REGISTER BEFORE BUILDING, per this class's rule and INV-linub's go\nprecedent (\"SIZE IT BEFORE BUILDING IT\"): the subject arms are sbt and lila,\nboth already surveyed at dev 285228adea/82f6dd89c5 under\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/t0_sizing_09092026/out/, so the B arm exists. A\ncontrol repo with no scala must be in the cohort, because sbt and lila BOTH\ncontain other languages and this measurement has already been burned once by\nrepo-wide roll-up (see the misattribution note in this item's filing)."  # 2ad6
